Cavitation and Bubble Dynamics — Christopher E. Brennen (@fd-cavitation: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_6GM4NG1BV40GS5D4SQCSAX2578
Christopher E. Brennen. Cavitation and Bubble Dynamics, Oxford University Press, 1995. [Caltech repository and complete files](https://authors.library.caltech.edu/records/4g53z-vj984) · [Institutional HTML edition](https://media.library.caltech.edu/CaltechBOOK:1995.001/bubble.htm).

Read the complete book for a sustained cavitation study; earlier steps use whole relevant sections on nuclei, bubble growth/collapse, oscillation, translation, bubbly mixtures and cavitating flow. Distinguish ideal pressure criteria from inception in real liquids and equipment.

The cited institutional edition is the 1995 work, not an inferred new edition from the repository update or later reprint. Free authorized full text is available; retain the book's copyright and component notices. Neither a pressure-drop calculation nor a bubble equation alone proves an apparatus will avoid damage. Source media remain external.

